            <fr:title text="(S+): the ledger conjecture">(S+): the ledger conjecture</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(S+). In the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> ledger
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[72 = 53 + \sum  c'_i + m_{\text {unknown}}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \sum  c'_i = 19 \iff  m_{\text {unknown}} = 0,
]]></fr:tex>
and either side implies <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Stated as a conjecture during the seventeenth pass and
discharged in the eighteenth: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c' = [5, 7, 7]]]></fr:tex>, so <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sum  c'_i = 19]]></fr:tex>
and the unknown count is zero. Kept as its own node because it is the
hinge the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex> argument turns on, and because a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 10]]></fr:tex> analogue
is the natural next ledger.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S): the n = 9 reduction</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal subsec:seventeenth (statement), subsec:eighteenth
(discharge); the jtype truncation bug found and fixed en route; commit
e8c7430.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
